      "writtenOn": "2025-04-08T11:50:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I feel that this could be improved a lot: Dawn doesn\u0027t want to care about `Limits` and chained descriptors at all and all these methods should work on `CombinedLimits` for simplicity. What we need though it is a single function `MaybeError UnpackLimitsIn(const Limits* limits, CombinedLimits* out);` that\u0027s used to validate the chained structs are the allowed one, and copies data in a `CombinedLimits`. This way internally all the code is consistent and doesn\u0027t need to care about the chain. (and doesn\u0027t need to care about what\u0027s allowed vs. not because that validation will have already been done).",
      "revId": "702c3cbc64622446e16ff085f2391096299445eb",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
